<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

However, there seems to be a small mistake in the logic of the assertion. The correct assertion should compare the new element at position `i` with the old element at position `i`, not `i-1`. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
